Package: casimir
Title: Catch Sampling Inference Methods in R
Version: 0.0.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("Henning", "Winker", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "henning.winker@fao.org"),
    person("Pedro", "Barros", role = "aut"))
Description: A catch estimator simulator for training in multi-stage
    landing-site surveys (catch assessment surveys). A spatial multispecies
    fishery with landing sites, fishing ranges by segment and a calendar
    (the logbook simulator of 'cpueTargeting') provides the true landings.
    Trainees design a stratified multi-stage survey (landing site x day,
    landings, species subsamples), draw samples with optional planted field
    artefacts, raise them to catch per species with the estimators of the
    FAO training, and compare designs by bias, precision and cost over
    replicates. Includes a 'shiny' app with a hide-truth switch for trainers.
